    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d772">

                <pb facs="0834" n="730" xml:id="pg730"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00 Revolutions/398: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Honduras</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-12-13T18:00:00-05:00">December 13,
                            1932—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>57. Your 110, December 11, 4 p.m. Department approves your statement to the
                    President and feels that the situation as at present reported does not warrant
                    the dispatch of a war vessel to Amapala.</p>
                <p>Please keep Department fully advised of developments at Amapala.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
